# `??` on an OWNING (`!`) param carrier — double-free, ASan-confirmed.
#
# `lower_expr`'s identifier arm peels a non-Copy param's pointer with
# `_t = copy _p.*`, leaving `_t` a SHALLOW copy of the pointee that does not own
# its payload (the typed provenance bit is `Local::deref_of_owning_param`). The
# `??` lowering's case-(a)/(b) discriminator tested the post-deref temp for
# Ptr-ness, saw a plain `Option[T]`, and took the "source owns its data" path —
# so the Move-extract zeroed only the COPY's payload field while the param's own
# slot kept pointing at the same Vector and stayed registered for drop. Both
# dropped.
#
# Fixed by reading the typed provenance instead of re-deriving the shape.
#
# ⚠ PLACEMENT: this fixture may NOT go top-level in `tests/fixtures/`. The
# self-host lane REJECTS `??` with a `Vector` payload
# (`E_DefaultOpRhsTypeMismatch`, re-measured this round), so a top-level
# placement would enter `runtime_parity_corpus` as a non-MATCH row and grow a
# ceiling Core #9 ⊕ forbids raising for a round's own inflow. The SH over-
# rejection is filed separately in `TODO.md`.
#
# RED-verified at the pre-fix compiler: RUN_RC 134, ASan
# `attempting double-free`. Expected stdout: `2` then `done`.
Vector[int] mkv(int n):
    Vector[int] v = []
    v.push(n)
    v.push(n)
    return v

Vector[int] fb():
    Vector[int] f = []
    f.push(9)
    return f

void take(Option[Vector[int]] ^o):
    Vector[int] got = o ?? fb()
    print(got.len())

void main():
    Option[Vector[int]] o = Some(mkv(7))
    take(^o)
    print("done")
